WEBVTT

00:00:00.992 --> 00:00:02.908
[PHOENIX] I'm Phoenix Wright,
a defense attorney.

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:05.033
While my reputation
has grown lately,

00:00:05.117 --> 00:00:07.492
there are still plenty
of challenges ahead of me.

00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:09.992
No matter the odds,
it's my job to stand up

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:12.242
for those who have no one
else in their corner.

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:14.283
I take the courtroom
again today,

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.700
to defend my client
and find the truth,

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:18.867
That's enough!

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.033
This trial has gone on
far too long.

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:23.367
The court sees
no reason to continue.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.283
[MAGGEY]
You can't be serious!

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.742
But I saw it!

00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:30.200
[MAGGEY]
There was another man!

00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:33.367
He's the real killer!

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.450
Why won't anyone believe me?!

00:00:37.992 --> 00:00:39.617
[JUDGE] I shall hereby
hand down the verdict

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.908
in the case against
Maggey Byrde.

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:45.325
Guilty as charged!

00:00:45.408 --> 00:00:47.117
[MAGGEY]
It wasn't me!

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.408
Heh.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.408
[PHOENIX]
New Year's cards?

00:02:24.492 --> 00:02:26.492
[MAYA] Well, it is
getting close to that time.

00:02:26.575 --> 00:02:28.742
And you gotta do your
part, so start writing!

00:02:31.492 --> 00:02:32.742
We could just print them.

00:02:32.825 --> 00:02:35.117
Hand-written's more personal!

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.825
I've been saying "thank you
for helping us to the very end,"

00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:39.575
so write that.

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:42.242
"Thank you for helping
us to the very end."

00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:44.617
Hmm? What do you mean,
"to the very end"?

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.908
That sounds like
we're closing up shop!

00:02:46.992 --> 00:02:48.033
Huh?

00:02:48.117 --> 00:02:49.617
You're hopeless.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.825
--[rumbling]
--[PHOENIX] Hmm?

00:02:50.908 --> 00:02:52.242
It's the cops!

00:02:52.325 --> 00:02:53.742
Woah, is something wrong?

00:02:53.825 --> 00:02:55.783
[GUMSHOE] No, I screamed my
head off cuz I felt like it!

00:02:55.867 --> 00:02:57.992
What's the deal with this?

00:02:58.075 --> 00:03:00.700
[MAYA] "Deadly Poisoning
Brings Guilty Verdict.

00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:03.575
Defense Attorney Wright...
Trounced"?!

00:03:06.158 --> 00:03:09.533
[PHOENIX] "The defense gave a
childishly amateur performance"?

00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:11.283
Wright must take full
responsibility for

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.033
the ruling in this case"?!

00:03:13.117 --> 00:03:14.450
I do?!

00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:15.908
[GUMSHOE] And all while
I was away scouting for clues

00:03:15.992 --> 00:03:18.533
and upholdin' justice.

00:03:18.617 --> 00:03:19.992
Here're your souvenirs.

00:03:20.075 --> 00:03:21.492
Oh, thanks, Dick.

00:03:21.575 --> 00:03:23.992
Don't change the subject!
What's this article all about?!

00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:26.742
[PHOENIX] I have no idea!
And you changed the subject!

00:03:26.825 --> 00:03:29.367
I'm stumped, too, and
this issue is a month old.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.283
Uh, more to the point,
I wasn't involved

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:32.867
in any poisoning cases lately.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.867
Ah!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.325
Everything about this is weird.

00:03:35.408 --> 00:03:38.117
If it wasn't you, then why
do people think it was?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.617
Wait, don't tell me.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.367
An imposter Nick?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.742
What? An imposter?

00:03:43.825 --> 00:03:45.117
[GUMSHOE]
Either way!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.450
You're comin' with me to
apologize to the defendant.

00:03:47.533 --> 00:03:49.783
And then you're gonna take
the case back to court.

00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:50.783
You got that?

00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:52.325
Hey, come on, calm down, man.

00:03:52.408 --> 00:03:54.033
Why are you getting
yourself so worked up?

00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:58.492
[GUMSHOE] Ah! Well. You'll get
it, when you see the defendant.

00:03:58.575 --> 00:04:02.242
Just help! It's your
responsibility to defend her!

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:04.533
That was odd.

00:04:04.617 --> 00:04:05.700
He's got a point.

00:04:05.783 --> 00:04:07.367
If this client entrusted
a case to my fake

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.408
based on my reputation,

00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:12.158
then I guess I kind
of am responsible.

00:04:12.242 --> 00:04:13.533
[PHOENIX]
And my impostor was willing to

00:04:13.617 --> 00:04:17.575
defend this client, huh?
I better find out who it is.

00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:24.783
[MAGGEY]
Ah! Mr. Wright!

00:04:24.867 --> 00:04:26.617
--It's you!
--[MAGGEY growls]

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.117
[MAYA]
Maggey?!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.408
[PHOENIX]
This is Maggey Byrde,

00:04:29.492 --> 00:04:32.658
a police officer
I defended once before.

00:04:32.742 --> 00:04:36.117
She was accused of murdering
her superior officer.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.033
What are you doing in here?

00:04:38.117 --> 00:04:39.408
I thought I got you acquitted!

00:04:39.492 --> 00:04:41.367
Oh, ha-ha, funny joke!

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.783
That fifth-rate defense job of
yours got me declared guilty!

00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:48.492
I understand why you're angry,
but let me explain!

00:04:48.575 --> 00:04:50.117
[MAGGEY]
A phony?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.367
I'm finding it kind
of hard to believe myself,

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.283
to be honest with you.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:55.367
[MAGGEY]
Looking back now,

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.242
I guess things did
feel a little off.

00:04:58.325 --> 00:04:59.242
A little?

00:04:59.325 --> 00:05:00.492
Yeah, just a little.

00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:01.908
Like how you were
a bit taller than normal,

00:05:01.992 --> 00:05:04.075
looked kind of shady,
your voice sounded sorta weird,

00:05:04.158 --> 00:05:06.117
and how you had
this funny accent.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.950
So the guy was nothing like me.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.158
Hang on a second, let me
tell you what was the same!

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:12.533
He had your spikey hair
and your blue suit!

00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:14.492
[MAYA] Those are your
signature features.

00:05:14.575 --> 00:05:15.825
Come on.

00:05:15.908 --> 00:05:18.283
By the way, how come
you're dressed like that?

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.033
After the incident
with the first murder,

00:05:20.117 --> 00:05:23.283
I quit the force and started
working at a restaurant!

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.867
That sounds like
a nice change of pace.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.200
Why don't you fill us in
on what happened?

00:05:28.283 --> 00:05:29.533
[MAGGEY sighs]
Yeah, sure.

00:05:29.617 --> 00:05:31.742
It all started last month.

00:05:31.825 --> 00:05:33.075
There were two men
at the restaurant,

00:05:33.158 --> 00:05:35.825
sharing a table
and drinking coffee.

00:05:35.908 --> 00:05:38.158
When, out of nowhere--
one of the men

00:05:38.242 --> 00:05:40.783
slipped some poison
into the other's cup.

00:05:40.867 --> 00:05:42.783
It only took one sip.

00:05:42.867 --> 00:05:43.908
[rasps]

00:05:43.992 --> 00:05:45.242
[gasps]

00:05:45.325 --> 00:05:46.367
[MAGGEY]
It was awful.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.825
I was so shocked.
I passed right out.

00:05:49.908 --> 00:05:51.742
[PHOENIX] Did you know
the victim personally?

00:05:51.825 --> 00:05:54.283
Not at all!
I'd never seen the guy before!

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.825
Lack of motivation
does help our case.

00:05:56.908 --> 00:05:59.367
And that mystery man
has to be the killer.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.700
Then why would
they convict poor Maggey?

00:06:01.783 --> 00:06:02.742
Because...

00:06:02.825 --> 00:06:04.492
...no one else saw it happen.

00:06:04.575 --> 00:06:06.200
[MAYA]
Really?

00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:09.867
[MAGGEY] The chef, the other
customer, everyone testified.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.283
They said the victim
was sitting alone

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.283
at his table the whole time!

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:14.617
Seriously?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.033
And then, to top it all off,

00:06:16.117 --> 00:06:17.617
they found a small
bottle of poison

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.283
in the pocket of my apron.

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.325
What? Why were
you carrying poison?

00:06:21.408 --> 00:06:23.658
It wasn't mine,
I don't know how it got there!

00:06:23.742 --> 00:06:26.325
Maybe the real killer it in when
I was passed out

00:06:26.408 --> 00:06:28.408
And this man no one else saw.

00:06:28.492 --> 00:06:30.075
You're sure he was there?

00:06:30.158 --> 00:06:31.658
[MAGGEY]
I'm dead sure!

00:06:31.742 --> 00:06:34.575
I mean, I was the one who took
the coffee over to their table!

00:06:34.658 --> 00:06:36.367
So what were these guys like?

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.908
Let's see. When I first saw
them, I thought they might be in

00:06:38.992 --> 00:06:40.825
the music industry or something.

00:06:40.908 --> 00:06:44.158
The victim was focusing
really hard on his earphone.

00:06:44.242 --> 00:06:48.200
And there was what looked
like a sample CD on the table.

00:06:48.283 --> 00:06:50.117
Was it an unmarked CD?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.783
[MAGGEY] No, it said
"MC"-something on it in marker.

00:06:53.867 --> 00:06:55.825
Must've been a band
preparing their debut.

00:06:55.908 --> 00:06:57.950
Like what's-his-face,
"MC Screwdriver?"

00:06:58.033 --> 00:06:59.950
I doubt it's
who you're thinking of.

00:07:00.033 --> 00:07:01.450
So Mr. Wright.

00:07:01.533 --> 00:07:03.825
Do you think it's
possible to get a retrial?

00:07:03.908 --> 00:07:05.033
[PHOENIX]
Mm-hmm.

00:07:05.117 --> 00:07:07.158
The defense attorney
lied about his identity.

00:07:07.242 --> 00:07:09.867
It shouldn't be much
trouble to get a do-over.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.658
[gasps] My life's been
a full course meal of bad luck,

00:07:12.742 --> 00:07:14.117
complete with
defeat for dessert.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.658
I've been hit by
all sorts of vehicles,

00:07:15.742 --> 00:07:17.575
gotten sick from every kind
of food, been falsely accused

00:07:17.658 --> 00:07:20.242
of murder twice,
and even landed a phony lawyer.

00:07:20.325 --> 00:07:21.700
Fake Nick!

00:07:21.783 --> 00:07:23.033
Why'd you have to do this?!
She's been through enough!

00:07:23.117 --> 00:07:24.367
Why're you glaring at me?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.658
I got through it all,
and I'll get through this!

00:07:26.742 --> 00:07:29.158
And one day,
I'll find the life I want.

00:07:29.242 --> 00:07:30.908
A normal and happy one!

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.408
[MAYA]
So inspirational.

00:07:32.492 --> 00:07:33.783
Maggey.

00:07:33.867 --> 00:07:36.367
Will you allow me to defend you,
this time for real?

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.117
Of course, Mr. Wright.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.617
I'm so glad!
Thank you for believing in me!

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.033
[PHOENIX] Whoever used
my name to frame her

00:07:43.117 --> 00:07:45.117
for murder had better watch out.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.283
We'll get 'em.

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:50.158
[MAYA]
Trés Bien, huh?

00:07:50.242 --> 00:07:52.825
Interesting place.

00:07:52.908 --> 00:07:54.158
[PHOENIX] Yeah, if you're
into suffocating from

00:07:54.242 --> 00:07:56.533
the overwhelming
scent of flowers.

00:07:56.617 --> 00:07:58.658
Is there not
a single person here?

00:07:58.742 --> 00:07:59.700
Hello--

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.533
[squeals]

00:08:01.617 --> 00:08:02.950
Sorry, didn't see you there!

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.033
[GIRL hums]

00:08:04.117 --> 00:08:05.408
[PHOENIX]
Hmm?

00:08:05.492 --> 00:08:08.283
[ARMSTRONG]
Ooh, la-la! We have guests!

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:09.700
<i>Bonjour</i> !

00:08:09.783 --> 00:08:10.783
Uh, hello, sir.

00:08:10.867 --> 00:08:12.158
[ARMSTRONG]
<i>Bienvenue!</i>

00:08:12.242 --> 00:08:14.658
Welcome to
<i>mon petite</i> restaurant!

00:08:14.742 --> 00:08:16.992
Oh, <i>monsieur</i> , what is
ze cause of such a face!

00:08:17.075 --> 00:08:18.367
I'm sorry?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.033
Like a puppy
rejected by life itself!

00:08:21.117 --> 00:08:23.033
You're fatigued, non?

00:08:23.117 --> 00:08:24.908
You need zis!

00:08:24.992 --> 00:08:26.950
Oil of bergamot.

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:29.325
With peppermint and clary sage.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.158
It will bring
out your very own...

00:08:32.242 --> 00:08:35.033
...natural beauty!

00:08:35.117 --> 00:08:36.992
Can't say that
was on my to-do list.

00:08:37.075 --> 00:08:40.283
Oh, well. If you will
be seated, Monsieur Wright.

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:41.825
Wait, how do you know my name?

00:08:41.908 --> 00:08:43.450
[ARMSTRONG] I could never
forget ze name of a man

00:08:43.533 --> 00:08:46.950
who flirted with me!
Especially in ze courtroom!

00:08:47.033 --> 00:08:49.950
I bet your imposter
cross-examined him in the trial.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:53.242
<i>Je m'appelle</i> Jean
Armstrong, ze chef here!

00:08:53.325 --> 00:08:54.783
Remember?

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.408
--[MAYA] Uh.
--[PHOENIX groans]

00:08:57.492 --> 00:08:59.242
[ARMSTRONG]
It was ze third of last month.

00:08:59.325 --> 00:09:01.950
Just after one in ze afternoon.

00:09:02.033 --> 00:09:05.617
A man enjoying a coffee
suddenly became violently ill.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.450
Because of the
poison in his coffee?

00:09:07.533 --> 00:09:09.992
[ARMSTRONG] Zat's right.
I was in ze kitchen.

00:09:10.075 --> 00:09:14.033
I heard ze sound of someone
collapsing and came running.

00:09:14.117 --> 00:09:16.950
Maggey had passed out.

00:09:17.033 --> 00:09:18.867
There should've been
another man at that table,

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.783
across from the one you saw.

00:09:20.867 --> 00:09:22.742
Yes, zat's what
Maggey is saying.

00:09:22.825 --> 00:09:25.950
And you're sure?
You didn't see anyone else?

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:27.950
Mon answer is ze same.

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:29.617
Zere was no one else zere.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.075
But that's not possible!

00:09:31.158 --> 00:09:34.283
[ARMSTRONG] Ze other customer
didn't see him, either.

00:09:34.367 --> 00:09:36.117
Honestly. I'm not
surprised she was

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.950
ze prime suspect
after what took place.

00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:40.492
[PHOENIX]
What do you mean by that?

00:09:40.575 --> 00:09:42.242
[ARMSTRONG]
Ze lottery ticket.

00:09:42.325 --> 00:09:43.617
How could you forget?

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.492
First I've heard of it.

00:09:45.575 --> 00:09:48.617
Ze man was listening
to ze radio with his earphone.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.992
In one ear.

00:09:50.075 --> 00:09:52.742
[PHOENIX] The earphone.
Maggey mentioned that, too.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.742
[ARMSTRONG] Ze winning number
was announced on ze news,

00:09:54.825 --> 00:09:57.700
I believe. Because all of
ze sudden he shouted!

00:09:57.783 --> 00:09:59.992
Five hundred grand! I won!

00:10:00.075 --> 00:10:00.992
Five hundred thousand?

00:10:01.075 --> 00:10:02.992
That's a whole lotta dolla!

00:10:03.075 --> 00:10:04.492
[ARMSTRONG]
Oui. And in ze court,

00:10:04.575 --> 00:10:06.325
zey said zat was her motive.

00:10:06.408 --> 00:10:10.242
She poisoned him to
take zat lottery ticket.

00:10:10.325 --> 00:10:11.492
[MAYA]
Oh, come on.

00:10:11.575 --> 00:10:13.492
I simply couldn't believe it.

00:10:13.575 --> 00:10:15.075
We don't believe it, either.

00:10:15.158 --> 00:10:16.908
That's why we're trying
to prove her innocence.

00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:19.325
But we need some sort
of lead to do that.

00:10:19.408 --> 00:10:20.742
Can you remember anything else?

00:10:20.825 --> 00:10:23.200
Anything at all could help.

00:10:23.283 --> 00:10:26.492
Let me think. Oh, zat's right.

00:10:26.575 --> 00:10:28.450
I remember zere was
a prescription bag

00:10:28.533 --> 00:10:30.325
on the table next to him.

00:10:30.408 --> 00:10:31.450
A prescription bag?

00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:32.742
Just sitting there?

00:10:32.825 --> 00:10:34.700
Oui. I just remembered.

00:10:34.783 --> 00:10:37.200
Did you happen to
mention that at the last trial?

00:10:37.283 --> 00:10:39.283
Non, non, I'd
forgotten all about it.

00:10:39.367 --> 00:10:40.617
That's our lead!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.825
[PHOENIX] Do you know what
kind of medicine it was?

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:44.367
<i>Lo siento.</i>

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.658
Now you're speaking Spanish.

00:10:46.742 --> 00:10:48.408
[PHOENIX]
Medicine.

00:10:48.492 --> 00:10:51.325
How is she?
Is Maggey doing all right?

00:10:51.408 --> 00:10:54.283
[PHOENIX] I wish I could
say she was, but not really.

00:10:54.367 --> 00:10:56.158
Understandable.

00:10:56.242 --> 00:10:57.825
I've been thinking
about her a lot,

00:10:57.908 --> 00:11:00.492
I've been so shorthanded
since I lost her!

00:11:00.575 --> 00:11:01.950
[MAYA]
But nobody's here.

00:11:02.033 --> 00:11:03.367
Say that louder, will yah?

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.492
[ARMSTRONG]
Mademoiselle! You pass ze test!

00:11:06.575 --> 00:11:08.658
Will you work
here starting tomorrow?

00:11:08.742 --> 00:11:10.367
Are you serious? Can I really?

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:11.867
You want to?!

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.992
Your style leaves
much to be desired,

00:11:14.075 --> 00:11:15.283
but your face is decent.

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:17.325
That's so sweet of you! Aww.

00:11:17.408 --> 00:11:20.325
Maya? Don't forget, we've got
Maggey's trial tomorrow!

00:11:20.408 --> 00:11:22.117
Zen come in afterwards!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.742
<i>S'il vous plait</i> !

00:11:23.825 --> 00:11:24.992
See-woo plate!

00:11:25.075 --> 00:11:27.908
Really? Why's this
exciting for you?

00:11:32.075 --> 00:11:33.825
[MAYA]
The trial's tomorrow morning.

00:11:33.908 --> 00:11:36.283
[PHOENIX] And we've found
ourselves a new clue.

00:11:36.367 --> 00:11:38.533
We have to believe our
client and do our best.

00:11:38.617 --> 00:11:41.283
[MAYA] Our big problem is that
everyone says the same thing.

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:44.242
Except for Maggey. That man...

00:11:44.325 --> 00:11:46.575
The man who disappeared. Yeah.

00:11:46.658 --> 00:11:48.367
[MAYA] And then there's
the winning lottery ticket,

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.242
and the poison in her pocket.

00:11:50.325 --> 00:11:52.617
You'll have to
fight off all of that.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.908
And I will. For Maggey.

00:11:54.992 --> 00:11:58.033
I can't let her be convicted on
a second false accusation.

00:11:58.117 --> 00:12:00.283
[MAYA] You know just what
to say to get me fired up!

00:12:00.367 --> 00:12:02.658
Let's do this! [giggles]

00:12:02.742 --> 00:12:03.700
[PHOENIX]
Hmm.

00:12:08.242 --> 00:12:11.533
[JUDGE] Court is now in session
for the trial of Maggey Byrde.

00:12:11.617 --> 00:12:12.992
Again.

00:12:13.075 --> 00:12:16.075
The defense is ready
to begin, Your Honor.

00:12:16.158 --> 00:12:18.408
[GODOT]
Mm. [slurps] Bitter.

00:12:18.492 --> 00:12:20.367
Now, then. Umm, Mr. Wright?

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.992
--[PHOENIX] Yes?
--[yekos]

00:12:22.075 --> 00:12:23.075
What are you doing?!

00:12:23.158 --> 00:12:24.867
Well, whenever I
addressed you last time,

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:26.700
you'd go, "Talkin' to me?!"

00:12:26.783 --> 00:12:28.700
So. Your politeness
shocked me a bit.

00:12:28.783 --> 00:12:31.075
Like I said,
that was an imposter.

00:12:32.033 --> 00:12:34.533
[GODOT] So, someone switched
out the pot for decaf.

00:12:34.617 --> 00:12:36.492
That doesn't matter.

00:12:36.575 --> 00:12:38.783
I wanna find out
if you're the real deal.

00:12:38.867 --> 00:12:40.700
Right here, right now.

00:12:40.783 --> 00:12:42.325
[PHOENIX growls]

00:12:42.408 --> 00:12:44.033
The court has
already given its verdict

00:12:44.117 --> 00:12:47.075
on this case once. However.

00:12:47.158 --> 00:12:50.075
Since there was an issue with
the defense's representation,

00:12:50.158 --> 00:12:52.450
we will now hold
a special retrial.

00:12:52.533 --> 00:12:55.325
The prosecution's
as real as it's ever been.

00:12:55.408 --> 00:12:56.950
Now why don't we get to work?

00:12:57.033 --> 00:12:58.658
I'd like to call a witness.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:04.867
I'm Dick Gumshoe, and
I'm a detective with the police.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.575
The victim's name was Glen Elg.

00:13:06.658 --> 00:13:08.825
He was a professional
programmer.

00:13:08.908 --> 00:13:11.867
The cause of death
was potassium cyanide poisoning.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.783
Traces of it were found
on the coffee cup

00:13:13.867 --> 00:13:15.367
the defendant
brought the victim.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.908
The defendant
has testified there was

00:13:16.992 --> 00:13:18.408
another man there.

00:13:18.492 --> 00:13:20.033
--At the table, sitting across
--[GUMSHOE] Yeah, yeah,

00:13:20.117 --> 00:13:21.200
--she did, she did!
--Yeah. But sadly,

00:13:21.283 --> 00:13:23.200
the chef and the
other customer

00:13:23.283 --> 00:13:24.408
have testified otherwise.

00:13:24.492 --> 00:13:26.367
--[gasps]
--Haven't they?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.908
That's correct. Their two
testimonies do line up on that.

00:13:29.992 --> 00:13:33.158
Both of 'em said there
was no other guy at the table.

00:13:33.242 --> 00:13:34.325
[MAGGEY sighs]

00:13:34.408 --> 00:13:36.242
Are we absolutely
certain the victim drank

00:13:36.325 --> 00:13:37.533
the coffee in question?

00:13:37.617 --> 00:13:39.492
[GODOT]
Hmph. See for yourself.

00:13:39.575 --> 00:13:42.158
[JUDGE] There is clearly
a coffee stain on the rim.

00:13:42.242 --> 00:13:44.825
[GODOT] That's a steaming
cup a' proof right there.

00:13:44.908 --> 00:13:46.908
He drank the coffee
the defendant brought him.

00:13:46.992 --> 00:13:48.950
[gulping]

00:13:49.033 --> 00:13:49.950
Like so!

00:13:50.033 --> 00:13:51.450
Okay, maybe, but...

00:13:51.533 --> 00:13:54.325
The defendant and victim
didn't know each other.

00:13:54.408 --> 00:13:55.867
She had no motive!

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.242
[GODOT] Five hundred thousand
bucks beg to differ.

00:13:58.325 --> 00:13:59.867
I didn't take that, I swear!

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:03.450
[GODOT] Detective! Where was
this lottery ticket recovered?

00:14:03.533 --> 00:14:04.992
On the defendant.

00:14:05.075 --> 00:14:07.783
When we patted her down right
after the incident happened.

00:14:07.867 --> 00:14:09.158
No way, it was?

00:14:09.242 --> 00:14:11.492
[MAGGEY]
Uh-uh. Mm-mm!

00:14:11.575 --> 00:14:12.533
Why don't we wrap this up

00:14:12.617 --> 00:14:15.492
with our final sip
of evidence?

00:14:15.575 --> 00:14:16.700
Take a look.

00:14:16.783 --> 00:14:18.200
[PHOENIX]
Did he say "sip"?

00:14:19.283 --> 00:14:20.367
[gasping]

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.158
This is the apron
the accused was wearing

00:14:22.242 --> 00:14:23.783
at the time of the murder.

00:14:23.867 --> 00:14:26.075
Yikes. That'll never come out.

00:14:26.158 --> 00:14:27.867
Yeah, but what is it?

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:31.075
[GODOT] The bottle of poison
was found in this pocket.

00:14:31.158 --> 00:14:32.658
That right, Detective?

00:14:32.742 --> 00:14:35.033
[GUMSHOE] Yeah, and
Maggey's, the defendant's prints

00:14:35.117 --> 00:14:36.783
were the only ones on it.

00:14:36.867 --> 00:14:40.950
[CROWD gasping, murmurin]

00:14:41.033 --> 00:14:42.450
Wait, that's it?

00:14:42.533 --> 00:14:45.158
You're not gonna mention
the huge red stain?

00:14:45.242 --> 00:14:46.742
[GODOT]
What stain?

00:14:46.825 --> 00:14:49.742
It could be blood,
but there's a lot there.

00:14:49.825 --> 00:14:51.408
No one told me!

00:14:51.492 --> 00:14:54.033
[PHOENIX] Can you see
anything out of that visor?

00:14:54.117 --> 00:14:56.742
[MAGGEY]
U-Um... It's not blood.

00:14:56.825 --> 00:14:58.075
It's just ketchup.

00:14:58.158 --> 00:14:59.492
[GODOT]
Huh?

00:14:59.575 --> 00:15:01.117
[MAGGEY] I got some on
my apron while carrying

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.533
a tray of breakfast
stuff to a table.

00:15:03.617 --> 00:15:06.575
[JUDGE] Refrain from
scaring us, defense.

00:15:06.658 --> 00:15:07.908
Pull a stunt like that again,

00:15:07.992 --> 00:15:09.575
and you'll be drinking
your joe through a straw.

00:15:09.658 --> 00:15:11.075
[PHOENIX]
Right. I'm sorry.

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.200
Order.

00:15:15.283 --> 00:15:17.242
I've yet to see anything that
makes me doubt the last verdict.

00:15:17.325 --> 00:15:18.742
--[gasps]
--Oh, no.

00:15:19.908 --> 00:15:20.825
You've got this!

00:15:20.908 --> 00:15:22.783
[PHOENIX]
Mm-hmm. Your Honor,

00:15:22.867 --> 00:15:23.825
the defense would
like to present

00:15:23.908 --> 00:15:26.325
new evidence to the court.

00:15:26.408 --> 00:15:27.408
Oh?

00:15:27.492 --> 00:15:29.742
We spoke to Trés Bien's
chef, Armstrong.

00:15:29.825 --> 00:15:32.117
He gave us some new information.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.158
[ARMSTRONG] I remember
zere was a prescription bag

00:15:34.242 --> 00:15:36.075
on ze table next to him.

00:15:36.158 --> 00:15:37.867
[JUDGE]
A prescription bag?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.158
This was indeed not deliberated
on during the last trial.

00:15:41.242 --> 00:15:42.867
I believe this
is an important piece of--

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.617
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.783
We've already investigated that.

00:15:48.283 --> 00:15:50.783
[GODOT] Yes, there was a
prescription bag at the scene.

00:15:50.867 --> 00:15:53.117
But it was empty.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.658
You already looked?

00:15:54.742 --> 00:15:55.825
We searched the scene,

00:15:55.908 --> 00:15:58.075
and couldn't find any
medicine anywhere.

00:15:58.158 --> 00:15:59.533
That's not good!

00:15:59.617 --> 00:16:00.658
Hold on.

00:16:00.742 --> 00:16:02.325
The victim was
poisoned to death!

00:16:02.408 --> 00:16:05.200
There's a chance the missing
medicine was laced with poison.

00:16:05.283 --> 00:16:07.533
Investigating this should
be our top priority.

00:16:07.617 --> 00:16:10.158
No complaints here,
let's investigate now.

00:16:10.242 --> 00:16:11.742
Read the bottom line.

00:16:11.825 --> 00:16:14.617
Ah. Otolaryngological?

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.742
Glen Elg got into
a fight with a coworker

00:16:16.825 --> 00:16:18.617
the day before the murder.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.533
During the altercation,
he suffered a blow to

00:16:20.617 --> 00:16:23.492
the side of the head and
ruptured his left eardrum.

00:16:23.575 --> 00:16:24.533
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:16:24.617 --> 00:16:26.075
His prescription
is applied topically

00:16:26.158 --> 00:16:27.533
to the inner ear.

00:16:27.617 --> 00:16:29.242
Not something to be ingested.

00:16:29.325 --> 00:16:32.075
What? You're kidding me!

00:16:32.158 --> 00:16:34.617
[GODOT]
Hmph. That settles it.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.575
You're obviously fake after all.

00:16:36.658 --> 00:16:39.700
[PHOENIX]
This is not going like I wanted.

00:16:39.783 --> 00:16:41.200
That's quite enough.

00:16:41.283 --> 00:16:43.825
This court sees no reason
to pursue the trial any longer

00:16:43.908 --> 00:16:45.325
than we already have.

00:16:45.408 --> 00:16:46.367
[GUMSHOE]
Hold it!

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:47.908
We haven't heard
from a witness yet!

00:16:47.992 --> 00:16:50.783
We can't conclude the trial
without hearing his testimony!

00:16:50.867 --> 00:16:52.200
Who's he mean?

00:16:52.283 --> 00:16:54.408
[JUDGE] We heard all
relevant testimony a month ago,

00:16:54.492 --> 00:16:55.700
did we not?

00:16:55.783 --> 00:16:57.950
The defense hasn't
cross-examined them!

00:16:58.033 --> 00:16:59.283
[JUDGE]
Hmm?

00:16:59.367 --> 00:17:01.117
Your Honor, I've arranged
a witness to the crime.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.158
No objections
from the prosecution.

00:17:04.242 --> 00:17:06.117
Detective Gumshoe!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.242
[GUMSHOE]
Hmm.

00:17:07.325 --> 00:17:08.492
So be it, then.

00:17:08.575 --> 00:17:10.492
Your witness may
approach the stand.

00:17:12.283 --> 00:17:14.200
The name is Victor Kudo.

00:17:14.283 --> 00:17:16.033
Born and bred in
the low-lying district,

00:17:16.117 --> 00:17:17.950
I'm a craftsman
through and through.

00:17:18.033 --> 00:17:19.617
At the time of the incident,

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.533
you were inside the
restaurant, weren't you?

00:17:21.617 --> 00:17:23.367
[KUDO] Uh-huh. Like I
said the last time,

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:26.117
I was eating some seeds over
a cup of javaccino.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:29.158
Victor. Will you tell
the court what you saw?

00:17:29.242 --> 00:17:30.200
We're eager to know.

00:17:30.283 --> 00:17:31.742
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

00:17:31.825 --> 00:17:34.117
Drinkin' a cup of javaccino
at that time had become

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:35.992
sort of a daily routine.

00:17:36.075 --> 00:17:38.325
So there I am, and
I see the serving girl slipping

00:17:38.408 --> 00:17:40.617
a white powder into
the guy's cup.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:41.908
And then...

00:17:44.867 --> 00:17:47.158
The man collapsed!

00:17:47.242 --> 00:17:49.575
And she was the girl I saw!

00:17:49.658 --> 00:17:51.033
Are you absolutely sure?

00:17:51.117 --> 00:17:52.992
[KUDO]
Of course! I wouldn't forget!

00:17:53.075 --> 00:17:54.533
She's got that uniform!

00:17:54.617 --> 00:17:55.575
Uniform?

00:17:55.658 --> 00:17:57.158
It's so revealing.

00:17:57.242 --> 00:17:58.575
I mean... What?

00:17:58.658 --> 00:18:01.533
Am I supposed to not look
at her legs in that getup?

00:18:01.617 --> 00:18:03.075
[chomping]

00:18:03.158 --> 00:18:04.783
I believe the
witness also remembers

00:18:04.867 --> 00:18:06.450
the victim well, no?

00:18:06.533 --> 00:18:07.533
My memory's great!

00:18:07.617 --> 00:18:09.700
If I'm wrong,
I'll sing like a bird

00:18:09.783 --> 00:18:11.658
and eat seeds at the same time!

00:18:11.742 --> 00:18:13.867
Okay, then. Go on.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.742
I remember all the details.

00:18:15.825 --> 00:18:18.700
The whole time, he kept rustling
the pages of his newspaper

00:18:18.783 --> 00:18:20.367
with his right hand.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.408
And while he did,
he gulped down his drink

00:18:22.492 --> 00:18:23.992
with his left hand.

00:18:24.075 --> 00:18:26.492
The left? But that can't be.

00:18:26.575 --> 00:18:27.825
What do you mean?

00:18:27.908 --> 00:18:29.617
The coffee stain
on the cup indicates

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:32.492
the victim drank with his
right hand, not his left.

00:18:32.575 --> 00:18:33.950
[gasping]

00:18:34.033 --> 00:18:36.783
Nah, you're wrong.
I remember it clear as day, kid!

00:18:36.867 --> 00:18:38.367
Wasn't he wearing
that weird blue lens

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.117
over his left eye ball?

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.492
That's correct.

00:18:41.575 --> 00:18:43.492
It's a small computer monitor
used by programmers,

00:18:43.575 --> 00:18:45.117
aptly called a "monocle."

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.325
Yeah! So like
I was saying before,

00:18:47.408 --> 00:18:49.325
he wore his earphone on
the same side as that thing

00:18:49.408 --> 00:18:51.033
and was listening to the radio!

00:18:51.117 --> 00:18:52.575
He messed with
it then used the same hand

00:18:52.658 --> 00:18:54.325
to drink his javaccino.

00:18:54.408 --> 00:18:55.450
[slurps]

00:18:55.533 --> 00:18:56.617
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.242
[PHOENIX]
That, sir, is impossible.

00:19:02.117 --> 00:19:05.700
[wails]
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:19:05.783 --> 00:19:08.242
The victim's left eardrum
had been ruptured.

00:19:08.325 --> 00:19:10.242
He got into a fight
the day before.

00:19:10.325 --> 00:19:12.200
He couldn't possibly
have worn his earphone

00:19:12.283 --> 00:19:14.742
in that ear.
He couldn't hear out of it!

00:19:14.825 --> 00:19:16.783
[KUDO]
Is that true?

00:19:16.867 --> 00:19:18.867
--It is.
--[KUDO] Buh-Birdie!

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:21.117
Pretty, pretty bird!

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.033
Your Honor,
this clearly sheds doubt

00:19:23.117 --> 00:19:25.908
on his memory, and his claim
that he saw the defendant.

00:19:25.992 --> 00:19:28.117
Oh, shut up! Whaddya you know?

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.325
I saw her! I got a
great look at her!

00:19:30.408 --> 00:19:31.575
In that case,
do you remember

00:19:31.658 --> 00:19:33.742
any distinctive features
about the waitress?

00:19:33.825 --> 00:19:35.700
You bet her beautiful butt I do!

00:19:35.783 --> 00:19:37.492
There was that
big ribbon in her hair.

00:19:37.575 --> 00:19:39.742
Her apron straps were
about to come undone.

00:19:39.825 --> 00:19:41.783
And then, of course,
there were those legs of hers.

00:19:41.867 --> 00:19:43.783
Couldn't help but get
a glimpse, you know?

00:19:43.867 --> 00:19:45.075
How's that?

00:19:45.158 --> 00:19:47.617
It's only stuff
you'd notice from behind.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.367
And what about her face?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.617
Did you see that at all?

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.533
Huh? Obviously, I saw her face!

00:19:52.617 --> 00:19:54.658
I don't know how to say this
without sounding like a jerk,

00:19:54.742 --> 00:19:56.783
but she was pretty
ordinary looking.

00:19:56.867 --> 00:19:58.408
Putting aside that
rude assessment,

00:19:58.492 --> 00:20:00.700
how could you not mention
my glasses you dog?

00:20:00.783 --> 00:20:02.117
I get the feeling
this guy didn't see

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.325
Maggey from the front.

00:20:03.408 --> 00:20:05.367
Or at least didn't
care to remember.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.825
[gasps]

00:20:08.908 --> 00:20:12.658
[PHOENIX] Mr. Kudo. Do you
recognize this apron?

00:20:12.742 --> 00:20:15.075
Yeah, that's the one they
use at the restaurant, right?

00:20:15.158 --> 00:20:16.325
[PHOENIX]
Have you seen this one?

00:20:16.408 --> 00:20:18.492
I never saw
one of them so filthy.

00:20:18.575 --> 00:20:19.992
[PHOENIX]
That's interesting.

00:20:20.075 --> 00:20:21.783
Because on the day
of the murder,

00:20:21.867 --> 00:20:23.908
the defendant
wore this very apron.

00:20:23.992 --> 00:20:25.033
Wait, she did?

00:20:25.117 --> 00:20:26.033
[gasps]

00:20:26.117 --> 00:20:27.867
Even if you forgot her face.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.575
You couldn't have forgotten
this bright red blemish.

00:20:30.658 --> 00:20:32.158
That is...

00:20:32.242 --> 00:20:34.408
...if you'd actually ever seen
the defendant from the front!

00:20:34.492 --> 00:20:36.408
[KUDO growls]
Shut your trap!

00:20:36.492 --> 00:20:38.242
My eyes were peeled
the entire time!

00:20:38.325 --> 00:20:40.367
Since I was only there for...

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:41.533
Her legs I assume?

00:20:41.617 --> 00:20:43.867
[KUDO whimpers]
Buh-buh-birdie!

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.450
Pretty, pretty bird!

00:20:45.533 --> 00:20:46.867
Order in the court.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.533
As the witness's
testimony seems suspect.

00:20:49.617 --> 00:20:52.742
I cannot, with good conscience,
pass a verdict at this time.

00:20:52.825 --> 00:20:54.408
I order the defense
and prosecution

00:20:54.492 --> 00:20:56.158
to investigate
this case further.

00:20:56.242 --> 00:20:58.200
Understood.

00:20:58.283 --> 00:20:59.367
[GODOT sighs]

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:00.783
[BOTH gasp, giggle]

00:21:00.867 --> 00:21:02.325
[sighs]

00:21:03.533 --> 00:21:06.242
And with that,
court is adjourned for now.

00:21:07.783 --> 00:21:09.033
[MAYA]
Way to go, Nick!

00:21:09.117 --> 00:21:10.408
You rocked it!

00:21:10.492 --> 00:21:12.283
You got the verdict
postponed to the next date!

00:21:12.367 --> 00:21:14.117
Not to mention
made Maggey's day!

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.658
But the question remains.

00:21:15.742 --> 00:21:18.242
How do we explain
the different testimonies?

00:21:18.325 --> 00:21:19.242
[MAYA]
Hmm?

00:21:19.325 --> 00:21:20.700
[PHOENIX]
That's a flashy color.

00:21:20.783 --> 00:21:22.492
And it's all beaten up.

00:21:22.575 --> 00:21:23.617
[TIGRE]
Hey!

00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:26.200
[MAYA]
What, what, what?!

00:21:26.283 --> 00:21:29.033
Whad'you think you're
doin' with my hot ride, sucker?

00:21:29.117 --> 00:21:30.408
I atta beat yah so hard,

00:21:30.492 --> 00:21:32.575
it'll feel like you were
smoochin' the express train!

00:21:32.658 --> 00:21:35.117
I'm sorry, man, I was
just checking it out!

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.825
[MAYA]
Um... Are you...

00:21:36.908 --> 00:21:38.367
...the imposter Nick?

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:39.950
--[gasps]
--Heh?

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:43.867
I don't gotta take this garbage.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.075
I atta beat you so hard,

00:21:45.158 --> 00:21:47.117
the express train'll
feel like pillows!

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.367
Uh...

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.492
[TIGRE]
I atta beat you so hard...

00:23:20.033 --> 00:23:22.075
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.158 --> 00:23:24.283
At Trés Bien,
the restaurant of mystery,

00:23:24.367 --> 00:23:26.283
Maya begins her part-time job!

00:23:26.367 --> 00:23:28.617
While we search for
the identity of my imposter,

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.617
a mysterious woman appears.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.825
As it turns out, it's possible
that a traffic accident

00:23:33.908 --> 00:23:35.783
had something to do
with the murder.

00:23:35.867 --> 00:23:38.783
The more we learn,
the more questions we have.

00:23:38.867 --> 00:23:41.367
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:44.825
Next episode: "Recipe
for Turnabout -- 2nd Trial"!

00:23:44.908 --> 00:23:46.033
Take that!
